        "original_id": "07047086-9d5a-5d7d-a5b2-389b34edb3c3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hudson Austin, Maurice Bishop, Bernard Coard, Eric Gairy\n- Organizations: New Jewel Movement\n- Places: Grenada\n- Roles: chairman, politician, general, leader\n- Events: 13 March 1979 revolution, coup, killing of Maurice Bishop, military government\n- Topics: socio-economic development, education, Black liberation\n\nFacts:\n- On 13 March 1979, the New Jewel Movement came to power in Grenada during a revolution that removed Eric Gairy from office.\n- Maurice Rupert Bishop was a Grenadian politician and the leader of the New Jewel Movement.\n- The New Jewel Movement promoted popular efforts in socio-economic development, education, and Black liberation.\n- Bernard Coard launched a coup within the revolutionary government and held power for three days.\n- General Hudson Austin deposed Bernard Coard after Coard’s three-day rule.\n- After the killing of Maurice Bishop, Hudson Austin formed a military government to rule Grenada and made himself its chairman.",
